      <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text);max-width:900px;line-height:1.7;">
        Over 53+ years, AXP has rewarded patient investors with a <strong>10.81% CAGR</strong> — beating the historical S&amp;P 500 average of ~10% despite significantly higher volatility (34.7% vs. ~15% for the index). The key risk is episodic: AXP's 2008–09 drawdown of 83.9% is among the most severe in large-cap financial history, requiring nearly 8 years to fully recover. Investors who held through crises were handsomely rewarded; those who sold near the trough locked in catastrophic losses. The <strong>recent 5-year CAGR of 21.7%</strong> reflects strong post-pandemic momentum but sits well above the stock's long-run average, suggesting mean-reversion risk.
